        "biography": "Sean Francis Bobbitt,\u00a0B.S.C.\u00a0(born 29 November 1958) is a\u00a0British\u00a0cinematographer, known for his collaborations with directors\u00a0Steve McQueen\u00a0and\u00a0Nia DaCosta. His accolades include nominations for an\u00a0Academy Award, four\u00a0British Academy Film Awards\u00a0and an\u00a0Emmy Award.\n\nHe was nominated for the\u00a0Academy Award for Best Cinematography\u00a0for his work on\u00a0Judas and the Black Messiah\u00a0(2021), which also earned him a BAFTA nomination. For\u00a0Sense & Sensibility (2008), he was nominated for the\u00a0Primetime Emmy Award\u00a0for Outstanding Cinematography.\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Sean Bobbitt, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia.",
